Description:
    Generates a reactive CRUD resource for a model that already exists.

    With no field list, the model's schema is used to determine columns, types,
    associations, and validators. Pass fields explicitly to override this or
    when the table hasn't been migrated yet.

    The generated index is live: search, filter, sort, and pagination are all
    reactive, edits happen in place, and changes from anywhere update every open
    list.

    Two models are MODIFIED. This one gets an after_commit broadcast. The
    related models get the missing has_many association and a ping so changes
    are reflected here. Existing declarations are left alone.

Example:
    bin/rails generate hibiki:rails:scaffold_controller Book

    This will create:
        app/models/book_query.rb
        app/channels/books_channel.rb
        app/channels/book_channel.rb
        app/forms/book_form.rb
        app/controllers/books_controller.rb
        app/views/books/*
        app/assets/stylesheets/hibiki_busy.css
    And modify:
        app/models/book.rb
        app/models/author.rb   # each model a belongs_to points at
        config/routes.rb

    Pass --phlex to emit Phlex components under app/views/books/*.rb instead of
    ERB templates. The view layer is the only thing it changes; it needs the
    phlex-rails gem and `bin/rails g phlex:install`.
